From 06516d8b0cb6f4817c5f91a0bc6c57c6059a1fb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:38:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tui): name who stopped a turn and leave a visible
 "Stopped by <login>" notice [daveey]

A client Stop (session.interrupt) from a remote login such as the Redde iPhone app
(basic:redde) ended the turn on a hidden empty row, so the chat went quiet and read as
stuck for hours. session.interrupt now logs by=<login>|Desktop with the peer, and an
interrupted turn persists a role=user display_kind=turn_stopped notice (display_text
'Stopped by <login>'); the Desktop renders it as a system line. System interrupts
(reapers, lease loss, shutdown) and completed turns add nothing.
